n  since he felt sorry he didn't have any  powers  in the show however the rod is given to  richard conrad aka blue bolt by the  island we never see blue bolt in the  present day hinting that he's either  dead or in hiding but since he has lost  this rod and now it's in the hands of  hutch  it's likely george had something to do  with this speaking of george the show  never goes into how he went from  sheldon's best friend and valiant member  of the union to the world's greatest  supervillain  in the comics george proposes to a girl  named sunny but is turned down because  she thinks he's too immature  and a playboy that could be why when  hutch asks the rod to send him to his  dad it always leads him to a strip club  a cheeky nod to his father's  philandering past in episode 8 we even  see an article which says  skyfox saving the world getting the  girls sunny ends up falling in love with  walter and george  can't take it he decides to live  incognito but he'll later learn that  walter was using his psychic powers on  sonny to make her fall in love with him  which of course  george does not like now there is a  sunny credited in episode one  she's the girl we see for a brief moment  in that fake world walt crates which he  uses to hold off the black star clone  either this is just a coincidence or  walt conjured her in this scenario from  a memory of his past  around the same time george becomes  disillusioned with the world he's helped  keep in balance particularly u.s  hegemony back in the day the world was  black and white you had the allies  versus the axes good versus bad but now  the world isn't so clear-cut  george ends up taking vice president  hubert humphrey hostage refusing to  release him until president lyndon  johnson ends the vietnam war  george believes he and the other heroes  have been nothing but pawns in an  establishment that undermines the  working class hence his eventual parting  with the union it's both philosophical  moral and personal wha